-- title:
--   Supersingular chart has q+1 ends, permuted by level automorphisms (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places that are rational, affine geometric, and whose value at the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$; let $s$ be a distinguished element of $W$. Assume the base-changed full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ (the kernel of the reduction of units $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$). Further data: intermediate fields $\mathbb Q \subseteq k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $k_0 \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, an element $\varpi_b$ of $A_b$; an algebra structure of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ on $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ under which the coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A) = \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,\kappa / (\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ is a domain; a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, an $A_b$-algebra, stable under every level automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a field $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ together with a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ to $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residue field $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, and such that every nonzero $f$ can be scaled into the integers with nonzero residue) with $B \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$; a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$; a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,C_s$, the fixed field of the subgroup of the Drinfeld $h$-action generated by $C_s$ inside the Drinfeld function field, whose image consists exactly of those elements of that fixed field lying in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$; and an isomorphism $e$ of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$-algebras from $F_{ss}$ onto this fixed field with $e(R.\mathrm{residue}(b)) = \rho(b)$ for all $b \in B$. Then there is a finite set $N$ of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with exactly $q+1$ elements such that a place $Q$ fails to lie in $N$ precisely when the residue of every element of $B$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and such that for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ ($\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ permutes $N$: for all $Q$, one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the count of the ends of a supersingular component in the stable reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$: the component is the Drinfeld curve $xy^q - x^qy = 1$ modulo the group $C_s$, and the places where the chart $B$ fails to be regular are its $q+1$ points at infinity, permuted by the level automorphisms. It feeds the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation rings and of the stalks at the base smooth points on the semistable-covering route.
